comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-18T19:18:11.981Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-18: active in one coupled SDK-first command-contract tranche spanning canonical flag concepts and budgets, truthful invocation arity, complete closed-domain recovery, refusal-closure scoring, source-derived executable recovery obligations, and shared CLI/MCP/completion/docs discovery metadata. This item is claimed because its acceptance surface will be edited and verified in this branch; unrelated parents and backlog items remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-18T21:13:36.921Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: the SDK now provides a typed recovery-closure scorer and findings, the gate registry runs a real temporary-tracker corpus, four current closed-domain probes score 4/4 (fraction 1.0), empty corpora fail closed, and omission/malformed-retry negative controls fail. Remaining acceptance: generate the exhaustive corpus from all contract tables, cover every subcommand family/required omission/mutual exclusion/error code, and persist a historical ratchet. Returning open and releasing ownership."
  "2026-08-18T21:49:08.769Z","harness:codex","Hosted CI evidence: PR #1061 exact head b953e36c22804ba26974a2c81307e91f1094f3ca passed the broad matrix except Gates (static), which correctly failed at generate-error-code-catalog.mjs --check because the recovery additions changed the reachable catalog. Treating this as gate-positive drift detection and regenerating through the repository-owned command."
  "2026-08-18T21:53:59.056Z","harness:codex","Hosted-gate correction evidence: pnpm contracts:errors:update synchronized both generated catalog partitions with 16 newly reachable recovery/lexicon/parity codes; pnpm contracts:errors:check passed; pnpm quality:static passed end to end, including 3043 lexicon entries, 2904/2904 observed flag parity, recovery closure 4/4 at 1.0, SDK snapshot/import-cost/transport checks, graph composition, and record integrity. The exhaustive-corpus remainder is unchanged, so returning this item to open and releasing ownership."
  "2026-08-18T23:41:26.210Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review evidence: flag-invocation-parity is now present in the exhaustive release automation inventory with its seeded arity negative control, and the inventory discovers its independently named executable. The committed registry, parity corpus, repository static gate, and exact full coverage all pass."
  "2026-08-19T01:01:52.369Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-19: review amendments make every current closed-domain get/search/list/context/next recovery preserve real positional operands through suggested_retry_args, use shell-safe display rendering, retain redaction through structured normalization, and require usage exit code. The executable corpus expanded from 4 to 8 probes and executes whitespace-bearing search retries without reparsing display text. Clean-room manual acceptance executed 6 CLI refusals/retries plus SDK get/search refusals and successful calls in an isolated tracker, then removed it. Final repository proof: 529/529 files and 7,586/7,586 tests pass; exact coverage is 55,439/55,439 statements, 41,357/41,357 branches, 11,473/11,473 functions, and 53,497/53,497 lines. quality:static passes including recovery closure 8/8, SDK surface governance, graph composition, and record integrity. Remaining feature acceptance is the generated exhaustive corpus, all error-code reachability, and historical ratchet, so this item will return open."
  "2026-08-19T04:10:06.315Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-19: replace the eight-row hand-maintained refusal gate with contract-generated probes, persisted ratchet data, required-argument/mutual-exclusion/domain coverage, and declared error-code reachability. This item is actively edited in the combined recovery-contract PR."
  "2026-08-19T05:28:37.686Z","harness:codex","Broad tranche evidence 2026-08-19: the hand-maintained refusal sample is replaced by an SDK-generated 18-contract corpus with a persisted historical minimum and required-probe ratchet. Scoring now verifies refusal exit, stable error code, complete allowed domain when required, shell-free retry argv, exact SDK-owned retry arguments, and actual retry success; seeded omission, malformed recovery, corpus regression, invalid JSON, and empty-corpus negative controls fail. Gate runtime tests retain one real end-to-end corpus execution and use focused injected negative controls instead of replaying the full CLI four times. Full 7,597-test exact coverage and quality:static pass. Honest residual: this tranche covers all core context-intent and read-projection closed domains plus their mutual exclusions, but the item's broader acceptance still asks for every closed-domain flag, every required-argument omission, every mutual-exclusion pair, and every declared repository error code; keep it open after delivery."
  "2026-08-19T05:47:18.405Z","harness:codex","Final tranche evidence 2026-08-19: the generated 18-probe closed-domain corpus executes real refusals and retries, requires exact error code/domain/retry arguments, fails omissions, and ratchets historical probe identities. Packed acceptance proves the public unknown_field_projection recovery envelope. Full 7,598-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and static assurance pass. Honest residual remains the item-wide census of every declared error code and every constrained flag family, so this feature must stay open after delivery."
  "2026-08-19T06:28:57.014Z","harness:codex","Final local pre-PR evidence 2026-08-19: the combined refusal closure implementation passes all 530 files and 7,598 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, the complete repository static assurance stack, ESLint, zero-clone detection, secret scanning, audit, and packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx acceptance. This feature remains actively claimed through hosted review because exhaustive every-code/every-domain refusal closure remains broader than this 18-probe tranche."
  "2026-08-19T06:30:31.787Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1062 at implementation commit a6df8f64a. Hosted checks and required bot review are running against the combined SDK/CLI recovery-contract, semantic lexicon, generated-surface, dependency, documentation, and PM-evidence tranche."
  "2026-08-19T07:42:39.040Z","harness:codex","Review-correction evidence 2026-08-19: list-family mutual-exclusion recovery now preserves the actual invoked command (including list-open), search recovery preserves the exact raw query including inline filters and spaces, and list projections canonicalize item.id/item.title aliases before deduplication so public rows cannot leak duplicate alias keys. New regression coverage exercises all three behaviors. Current-tree proof passes 531/531 files and 7,600/7,600 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (55,585 statements, 41,480 branches, 11,517 functions, 53,631 lines), repository static assurance, the isolated six-operation transport floor, secrets, and zero-vulnerability audit. A disposable tracker executed the emitted list-open and search retry argv successfully; packed npx acceptance also passed. The broader every-domain/every-error census remains honest residual, so this item stays active through review and will return open afterward."
  "2026-08-19T08:39:05.851Z","harness:codex","Second hosted review remediation evidence: preserved the CLI derived-index fast path by classifying projectionCommand and Commander negation defaults as non-semantic while normalized true filters still force source fallback; mapped search-contracts error provenance to search; made --full semantic resolution fail closed; exposed a stable ItemMetadataKey union without breaking ITEM_METADATA_KEY_ORDER consumers; and added real CLI/generator negative controls. Verification: 531 files / 7601 tests passed with exact statements 55590/55590, branches 41486/41486, functions 11517/11517, lines 53636/53636; pnpm lint passed with ESLint, zero jscpd clones, 100% docstring/static assurance, contract, graph, record-integrity, token, and recovery gates."
  "2026-08-19T10:05:45.625Z","harness:codex","Reviewed-head handoff 2026-08-19: all review findings in this tranche are fixed, including source-preserving retries, exact search provenance, fail-closed semantic mapping, persistent-index eligibility, and stronger offset/help assertions. Full proof is 531 files / 7,602 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 plus quality:static. The generated corpus still does not census every declared error code and every constrained domain, so this feature returns open and unclaimed rather than being falsely closed."
  "2026-08-19T16:37:08.524Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-19: selected after a complete all-status 2,524-item inventory (2,190 closed, 320 open, 14 canceled), focused duplicate searches, full live metadata/comments/history/relationship reads, and GitHub issue lineage verification. This item is actively edited in one coupled SDK-first recurrence and executable-guidance PR spanning lifecycle primitives, CLI/MCP contracts, immutable history, capability-aware hints, generated agent guidance, recovery assurance, docs, exact coverage, and temporary installed-consumer acceptance. Unrelated backlog items remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-19T18:27:48.610Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: recovery closure remains complete at 18/18 probes; flag/gate contracts, 198 closed-domain and CLI guidance tests, 44 lexicon/catalog/list tests, and the complete 7,618-test exact coverage run passed. The reorganized recovery suite passed 12/12 after its obsolete linked path was replaced. The broader closure-metric program retains residual domains and remains open for later tranches."
  "2026-08-19T19:20:11.180Z","harness:codex","Pull request evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1063 carries the reviewed SDK, CLI, MCP, contract, documentation, test, changelog, and tracker delivery at exact head 1d85f3a0d."
  "2026-08-20T04:53:17.899Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-20: actively extending the recovery-closure corpus with generated tracker-preflight states and real isolated retries. The new shared guard will expose missing-root, non-directory-root, and settings-missing refusals with structured legal recovery; the gate will score and execute them rather than asserting prose."
  "2026-08-20T06:14:26.106Z","harness:codex","2026-08-20 tranche evidence: tracker filesystem preflight adds three generated executable contracts to the recovery corpus, raising it from 18 to 21 probes. Real isolated retries initialize missing and empty roots; a regular-file root executes a safe alternate-root retry and proves no unsafe init recommendation. Scorer negative controls cover missing probes, code/exit/recovery-kind mismatches, missing init argv, unsafe init, failed retry, malformed envelopes, empty corpus, and ratchet regression. Full exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and packed acceptance pass. Honest residual remains the item-wide census of every closed domain, required omission, mutual exclusion, and declared error code, so this feature returns open."
  "2026-08-20T06:30:11.738Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1065 at implementation head 3a83a155f advances the executable recovery corpus from 18 to 21 with three tracker filesystem states while preserving the honest exhaustive-census residual."
  "2026-08-20T07:32:56.192Z","harness:codex","PR #1065 review evidence: umbrella recovery contracts now include the fourth unreadable-root state, explicit selected-root init retries, fail-closed malformed inputs, replayable append-only test metadata, and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 7,635 tests. The feature remains open for later independently scoped recovery work after this reviewed delivery."
  "2026-08-21T22:48:10.211Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-22: one coupled SDK/CLI/contract/assurance tranche will declare binding diagnostic ceilings, preserve corrective actions through deterministic degradation, replay the ten most frequent refusal paths in isolated trackers, and extend executable recovery evidence. Only these four actively edited items are claimed; all other backlog items remain unclaimed."
  "2026-08-21T23:58:53.188Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence (2026-08-22): extended executable recovery closure with action-first diagnostic projection, required-action preservation, deterministic degradation receipts, a 10-probe governed diagnostic corpus, and negative controls for missing corrective action and invalid receipts. Refusal closure passed 22/22 and diagnostic output passed 10/10; diagnostic corpus measured 5,709 estimated tokens and no findings. Full lint/static assurance, 7,717-test exact 100% coverage, security scan/audit, packed npx, and isolated Node/bunx validation passed. Item remains active because its acceptance criteria require exhaustive runtime coverage of every remaining documented domain/error code."
learnings[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-19T05:28:38.341Z","harness:codex","Executable assurance should run the full real corpus once, then exercise failure classification through deterministic injected observations. Replaying an expensive corpus for each scorer branch adds latency without improving behavioral evidence."
  "2026-08-19T08:39:06.383Z","harness:codex","Adapter-only enumerable options can silently defeat SDK fast paths even when behavior remains correct. Pin the real CLI registration path against corrupted source files so derived-index use is observable, and treat raw Commander negation defaults as non-semantic only after normalized filters preserve requested fallback semantics."
  "2026-08-19T18:27:49.965Z","harness:codex",Recovery metrics stay trustworthy only when executable linked tests evolve with repository structure and the umbrella distinguishes completed tranches from residual scope.
  "2026-08-21T23:59:02.159Z","harness:codex",A recovery-closure corpus must validate both the presence of a recovery object and a usable corrective action. Negative controls for missing actions and forged/inconsistent degradation receipts prevent superficially structured diagnostics from passing.
